--- E. BSD index bookkeeping ---
ellbsd doc: L'(E,1) = c*R*S with R = hhat(P0) (generator), S = |Sha|.  G = n P0 + tors => hhat(G) = n^2 R.
=> L'/(c*hhat(G)) = S/n^2.  Computed value 1 (38 digits) => S = n^2 under BSD, NOT S*n^2 = 1.
with ellsaturation(1000): n = 1 or n > 997 ; under BSD: n = 1 <=> Sha trivial ; n>997 <=> |Sha| > 994009.
largest prime below 10^4 = 9973 ; with ellsaturation(10000): n = 1 or n > 9973 ; then hhat(P0) = hG/n^2 < hG/10^8 = 1.5187e-08 (= 1.5188/10^8)
